CQ number 12 for the demcare ontology is: What sleep-related situations indicate a problem or possibly problematic condition?

SELECT ?problem ?problemLabel WHERE {
  ?problem a <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#SleepProblem> .
  OPTIONAL { ?problem rdfs:label ?problemLabel . }
}

This query retrieves all classes that are subclasses of SleepProblem, which represent sleep-related situations indicating a problem or possibly problematic condition, such as <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#SleepDurationProblem>, <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#SleepEfficiencyProblem>, <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#SleepLatencyProblem>, <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#FragmentedSleepProblem>, <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#Nocturia>, <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#PeriodicLimbMovement>, <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#NappingProblem>, and <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#InterruptedSleepProblem>.

CQ number 27 for the demcare ontology is: What functional areas are of clinical relevance?

SELECT DISTINCT ?functionalArea WHERE {
  ?assessment a <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#FunctionalAbilityAssessment> .
  ?record <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#containsAssessment> ?assessment .
  ?functionalArea a <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#FunctionalAbilitiesData> .
}

CQ number 29 for the demcare ontology is: What activities (situations) are of concern (i.e., highlighted) for a given patient?

SPARQL query:

PREFIX ns0: <http://www.demcare.eu/ontologies/combined.owl#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>

SELECT ?event ?eventType
WHERE {
  ?event a ?eventType ;
         ns0:highlight true ;
         ns0:hasAgent ?patient .
  ?patient a ns0:Patient .
}

This query retrieves all events (activities or situations) that are highlighted (of concern) for a given patient, along with their types.

